
titre $ Key to the taxa of Oudemansiella [Square brackets indicate specimens not treated in this monograph]
com$ Petersen & Hughes  2010 : The Xerula/Oudemansiella Complex  p271/ adapt GF dec2010
1,0$Type species: O. platensis Spegazzini [non O. Canarii. Clemençon. 1979. Sydowia 32: 78]/// Basidiomata resembling Tricholomopsis, Armillaria tabescens, Rhodotus, Ossicaulis, Cyptotrama, Hypsizgus, fruiting on exposed rotting wood (i.e. logs, branches). Pileus dry to commonly viscid. usually with scattered floccules resembling veil fragments. Lamellae white to off-white, usually subdistant. somewhat ventricose, not marginate. ///Stipe central. with insertion usually inflated into a pad or knot: veil absent. rudimentary, fugacious or (unusually) membranous and persistent. Pileipellis a polycystoderm or ixotrichodermium constructed of hyphal chains with cells subspherical, keg-shaped, narrowly fusiform, filamentous. broadly or narrowly rod-shaped. Basidiospores large, globose to subglobose, appearing thick-walled, white in prints./// Pleuro- and cheilocystidia well-developed. 


1,0 $ Pileus sky blue, deeply sulcate-striate; pileipellis an ixoparalleloderm; central Africa.$ 6. O. linicolor
1,0,n $ [cheilocystidia 37-64 x 13-30 µm, clavate to broadly clavate: spores 17.5-21.5 x 17-20 µm (L" = 19.4 µm)
1,2 $ Pileus white, yellowish, pinkish to fuscous; pileipellis not an ixoparalleloderm; annulus present or lacking
2,3 $ Pileipellis a hymeniderm of inflated, pedicellate cells profilerating into a polycystoderm, trichodenn or disarticulating ixotrichoderm
2,9 $ Pileipellis a hymeniderm of inflated, pedicellate cells without successive polycystoderm or disarticulating ixotrichoderm
3,4 $ Pileipellis a polycystoderm of chains of keg-shaped or subspherical cells: annulus lacking
3,8 $ Pileipellis a trichoderm or an ixotrichoderm of erect or tangled hyphae, sometimes disarticulating; annulus present or absent
4,5 $ Pleurocystidia inflated proximally with significantly extended neck
4,6 $ Pleurocystidia utriform to paddle-shaped: Pacific Rim
5,0 $ Caribbean. Central and South America: spores 15-17 x 14-16 µm (L" = 16.4 µm); pileus surface with scattered flocccules $4. O. cubensis
5,0 $ Antipodes to Sri Lanka: spores 22-25 x 20-24 µm (L" = 22.8 µm): pileus apparently dry. without floccules $ 1. O. apalosarca
6,0 $ [ Basidiospores 9.5-11.5 x 7.0-8.5 µm (Q'" = 1.38: L''' = 10.38 µm), ellipsoid; pleurocystidia paddle-shaped. 50-79 x 22-27 µm. with large apical refringent-resinous deposit: pileus ruddy-brown without floccules, reticulate- wrinkled; Papua New Guinea ] $ ZT 71-203]
6,7 $ Basidiospores larger, globose to subglobose
7,0 $ [Australia: spores 19-26 x 18-25 µm (L" = 22.2 µm); pleurocystidia paddleshaped. 130-158 x 35-42 µm. long-pedicellate: pileus -10 mm broad. apparently dry ]$ TENN 537761
7,0,n $ [cheilocystidia -130 pm long. cylindrical, conspicuouly clamped ]
7,0 $ Southwestern China; spores 33-39 x 30-35 µm (L'' = 35.9 µm) pleurocystidia broad Iy cy lindrical to utriform. 170-220 x 41-55 µm. pedicellate; pileus -40 mm broad. apparently dry. . $ 9. 0. Yunnanensi,1
8,0 $ Pileus viscid. dark umber with scattered floccules when young. paler to whitish or pinkish on expansion: pi leipellis a disarticulating trichodermium, with rod-shaped terminal cells: cheilocystidia 38-74 x I J-26 µm, clavate to fusiform: spores 19-25 x 18-23 µm (L'" = 21.8 µm): New and Old World tropics $2. O. canam
8,0 $ Pileus thinly viscid. laccate when dried. without floccules: pileipellis hyphae lax, undulating. tilamentous to very narrowly clavate. rarely disarticulating: cheilocystidia 42-87 x 10-19pm. narrowly clavate to cylindrical; spores 17-22 x 17-21 pm (L" =20.3 µm): eastern Australia $5. O. exannulata
9,0 $ [Pileipellis an ixohymenoderm of irregularly coralloid hyphae with some clavate (not broadly fusiform) pileocystidial apices: pileus with thick viscid surface layer: annulus prominent ] $O. Mucidula
9,10 $ Pileipellis composed of cyme-like branches of subterminal cells: terminal cells clavate. broadly clavate or lobatc: annulus present or absent (0. sub-mucida complex)
10,11 $ Pileipellis generally poorly organized; pileocystidia narrowly clavate, fusiform to lobate
10,0 $ Pileipellis a well-developed hymeniderm of broadly fusiform to sphaeropedunculate pileocystidia $ 7. O. submucida
10,0,n $[pileus oily-viscid, white to pale ochraceous; pleurocystidia with prolonged neck; spores 18-25 x 17.5- 23 µm(Q''' = I .14). broadly ovate; Malaysia, China, Bhutan] (pileus dry, North Borneo var. persicca)
11,0 $ Annulus absent; North Borneo; pleurocystidia thin-walled; pileus -30 mm broad, white; lamellae white; spores 21-28 x 19-24 µm $ 3. O. crassifolia
11,0 $ [Annulus present; Puerto Rico; pleurocystidia thick-walled; pileus -44 mm broad, yellow-brown to pinkish brown with brown disc; lamellae pale pinkish buff; spores -17 x 16 µm (species incertae cedis)] $ O. fibrillosa
